{% comment %} Accordion rows. One row = one capture + one render line. Write plain text: Enter once = new line, an empty line = new paragraph. {% endcomment %}
{% capture a1 %}
Knees are made to move, and they stiffen when they rest. When they're stiff, you move less. When you move less, they get stiffer. That's <strong>the rest trap</strong>.

This rub is made to get you out of it: <strong>cool, then warm,</strong> within a minute, and gentle enough for <strong>every morning and evening</strong>, so moving becomes the easy part of your day again.

100 g · [lasts about X weeks at twice a day]
{% endcapture %}
{% render 'boarage-accordion-item', title: 'Description', content: a1, id: 'faq-1', margin_top: 16, open: true, box_color: '#ffffff', border_color: '#dfe6e2', icon_color: '#1d4d36', title_color: '#1d4d36', text_color: '#1d4d36', bullet_color: '#2fbd44', title_size: 19, text_size: 17 %}
{% capture a2 %}
<strong>Day 1:</strong> you feel it in the first minute, and write down three things you've quietly given up.
<strong>Weeks 1–4:</strong> the minute you look forward to, every morning and evening.
<strong>Weeks 5–8:</strong> the minute starts leading somewhere: the walk, the stairs, the garden.
<strong>Weeks 9–12:</strong> around day 66 it sticks, and you stop thinking twice.
{% endcapture %}
